1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,289
In Orchard Core, a taxonomy is a managed list of terms that you

2
00:00:05,289 --> 00:00:07,278
use to categorize content.

3
00:00:07,278 --> 00:00:11,567
In this video, you create a taxonomy, add terms to it, edit and

4
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:15,980
delete them, arrange them in a hierarchy, and publish the result.

5
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:25,576
A taxonomy is a content item that holds a list of terms, such as Topics.

6
00:00:25,576 --> 00:00:30,123
A term can contain other terms, which gives the list a hierarchy.

7
00:00:30,123 --> 00:00:34,670
Every term is a content item of one content type that you choose.

8
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:38,999
The taxonomy that you build in this video is called Topics.

9
00:00:38,999 --> 00:00:42,963
It has two terms at the top level, Gardening and Cooking, and each

10
00:00:42,963 --> 00:00:45,000
of them holds terms of its own.

11
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:50,237
The terms are stored inside the taxonomy, and are not listed as content

12
00:00:50,237 --> 00:00:51,694
items of their own.

13
00:00:51,694 --> 00:00:56,007
Adding, editing, and deleting terms changes a draft of the taxonomy.

14
00:00:56,007 --> 00:00:59,620
The published taxonomy changes only when you publish it.

15
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:05,169
Before you start, enable the Taxonomies feature in Tools, Features.

16
00:01:05,169 --> 00:01:12,270
Adding, editing, and deleting terms needs the Manage taxonomies permission, which administrators have.

17
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,972
The terms need a content type.

18
00:01:14,972 --> 00:01:18,225
This site has one named Topic, which has only a title.

19
00:01:18,225 --> 00:01:21,370
A separate video shows how to create a content type.

20
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:32,384
Content, Content Items lists the content of your site, and its New button creates content items.

21
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:34,771
Select New, and then Taxonomy.

22
00:01:34,771 --> 00:01:39,280
A taxonomy is a content item, so you create it like any other.

23
00:01:39,806 --> 00:01:43,253
The editor has a title, an alias, and a permalink.

24
00:01:43,253 --> 00:01:45,530
Let's type Topics as the title.

25
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:48,976
The alias and the permalink are generated from it.

26
00:01:49,455 --> 00:01:54,025
Term Content Type sets the content type of the terms, and it is required.

27
00:01:54,025 --> 00:01:59,579
The list leaves out special-purpose content types that have a stereotype, such as widgets.

28
00:01:59,579 --> 00:02:01,025
Let's select Topic.

29
00:02:01,507 --> 00:02:02,832
Select Publish.

30
00:02:02,832 --> 00:02:07,500
The taxonomy is saved, and Topics appears in the list as a Taxonomy.

31
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:11,537
A taxonomy has to be saved before you can add terms to it.

32
00:02:15,739 --> 00:02:17,697
Open Topics from the list.

33
00:02:17,697 --> 00:02:22,469
Since the taxonomy is saved, its editor shows an Add Topic button, named

34
00:02:22,469 --> 00:02:24,549
after the term content type.

35
00:02:25,026 --> 00:02:26,475
Select Add Topic.

36
00:02:26,475 --> 00:02:31,578
The editor of a Topic asks for a title, so type Cooking and select Publish.

37
00:02:31,578 --> 00:02:36,806
That adds the term to a draft of the taxonomy, not to the published taxonomy.

38
00:02:37,284 --> 00:02:41,835
The term appears in the list, with an Edit, an Add, and a Delete button.

39
00:02:41,835 --> 00:02:45,161
Add a second term at the top level in the same way:

40
00:02:45,161 --> 00:02:46,094
Gardening.

41
00:02:46,562 --> 00:02:50,759
To put a term inside another term, select the Add button on its row.

42
00:02:50,759 --> 00:02:52,687
Let's add Baking to Cooking.

43
00:02:52,687 --> 00:02:55,182
The term is indented below its parent.

44
00:02:55,657 --> 00:02:58,810
Add Grilling and Roasting to Cooking in the same way.

45
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:02,819
Each term is placed after the terms that its parent already holds, so

46
00:03:02,819 --> 00:03:06,027
the list follows the order in which you add the terms.

47
00:03:06,490 --> 00:03:10,132
Select the Add button on the Gardening row to add Vegetables.

48
00:03:10,132 --> 00:03:13,936
Then select Add Topic to add Herbs at the top level, even though

49
00:03:13,936 --> 00:03:15,675
it belongs with Gardening.

50
00:03:15,675 --> 00:03:17,360
A later chapter moves it.

51
00:03:21,598 --> 00:03:25,513
In the Topics editor, select Edit on a row to change a term.

52
00:03:25,513 --> 00:03:29,072
Let's rename Grilling to Barbecue, and select Publish.

53
00:03:29,072 --> 00:03:31,918
The term keeps its place in the hierarchy.

54
00:03:32,381 --> 00:03:35,396
To remove a term, select Delete on its row.

55
00:03:35,396 --> 00:03:37,118
Let's delete Roasting.

56
00:03:37,118 --> 00:03:39,271
A dialog asks you to confirm.

57
00:03:39,723 --> 00:03:40,638
Select Ok.

58
00:03:40,638 --> 00:03:43,838
A message says Taxonomy item deleted successfully.

59
00:03:43,838 --> 00:03:48,239
Deleting a term also deletes the terms inside it, so check the children

60
00:03:48,239 --> 00:03:50,353
of a term before you delete it.

61
00:03:54,549 --> 00:03:58,701
In the Topics editor, drag a term by its row to change the order.

62
00:03:58,701 --> 00:04:01,099
Let's drag Gardening above Cooking.

63
00:04:01,099 --> 00:04:03,789
The terms inside Gardening move with it.

64
00:04:04,564 --> 00:04:08,538
Dragging a term to the right moves it a level deeper, and dragging

65
00:04:08,538 --> 00:04:10,800
it to the left moves it a level up.

66
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:16,154
Let's drag Herbs below Vegetables, and a little to the right, to place it inside Gardening.

67
00:04:16,643 --> 00:04:19,518
The order is stored when you save the taxonomy.

68
00:04:19,518 --> 00:04:22,610
Until then, the page warns you before you leave it.

69
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:25,593
Select Save Draft to keep the order in the draft.

70
00:04:29,790 --> 00:04:32,745
Every change to the terms is kept in a draft.

71
00:04:32,745 --> 00:04:37,091
In the Content Items list, Topics shows a Published badge and a Draft

72
00:04:37,091 --> 00:04:39,410
badge, since it has both versions.

73
00:04:39,864 --> 00:04:40,824
Open Topics.

74
00:04:40,824 --> 00:04:44,822
The terms are in the order that you saved, but the published taxonomy

75
00:04:44,822 --> 00:04:46,634
does not hold these changes.

76
00:04:47,092 --> 00:04:48,226
Select Publish.

77
00:04:48,226 --> 00:04:52,657
The message says Your Taxonomy has been published, and the list shows Topics

78
00:04:52,657 --> 00:04:54,602
with only the Published badge.

79
00:04:56,602 --> 00:04:58,633
That's how a taxonomy works:

80
00:04:58,633 --> 00:05:02,936
it is a content item whose terms you add, edit, delete, arrange in

81
00:05:02,936 --> 00:05:04,788
a hierarchy, and publish.

82
00:05:04,788 --> 00:05:06,342
Thanks for watching.

